  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Investing towards Malaria Elimination - Eritrea (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Eritrea, Malaria, Ministry of Health of the State of Eritrea (MOH)This program has the following goals: Reduce incidence of malaria cases and deaths by 50% from 2010 levels by 2017 and bring Test Positivity Rate (TPR) below 5% required for pre-elimination by 2017. The objectives of this program are: By 2019, 100% of fever cases presenting to health providers shall be promptly tested for malaria , and 100% of the confirmed malaria cases treated according to national guidelines.  By 2019, strengthen malaria surveillance system in light of pre-elimination; and detect and respond to 100% malaria epidemics within two weeks of onset.  Develop requisite capacity in program management at all levels in order to achieve malaria pre-elimination objectives.  Increase average number of LLINs per household from 1.8 to 2.5 by 2015 and beyond.  Increase percent of &lt;5 children with fever seeking treatment within 24 hours from 26.8% to 50% by 2019.  Increase percent of population sleeping under LLINs from 60% to 80% by 2019.  Increase percent of targeted houses sprayed with insecticides from 86% to 95% by 2015 and beyond.  Increase proportion of household members participating in environmental management activities from 84% to 100%</narrative>
  </description>
